# ==============================================================================
# ClauseLens Deontic Knowledge Base & Domain Axioms
# Predicates:
#   Obl(party, action)  : party is obligated to perform action
#   Perm(party, action) : party is permitted to perform action
#   Forb(party, action) : party is forbidden from performing action
# ==============================================================================

# Axiom 1: Obligation implies Permission (Deontic Subordination)
# If a party is obligated to do an action, they are inherently permitted to do it.
forall p, a: (Obl(p, a) -> Perm(p, a))

# Axiom 2: Permission and Prohibition are mutually exclusive (Duality)
# A party cannot be simultaneously permitted and forbidden to perform an action.
forall p, a: ~(Perm(p, a) & Forb(p, a))

# Axiom 3: Obligation and Prohibition are contradictory
# A party cannot be simultaneously obligated and forbidden to perform an action.
forall p, a: ~(Obl(p, a) & Forb(p, a))

# Axiom 4: Prohibition equivalence
# Being forbidden is equivalent to not being permitted.
forall p, a: (Forb(p, a) <-> ~Perm(p, a))

# ==============================================================================
# Action Conflict Pairs
# Actions that cannot be simultaneously permitted or obligated.
# ==============================================================================

# Axiom 5: Unrestricted Entry vs Prior Notice Obligation
# Entering without notice contradicts requiring prior notice.
forall p: ~(Perm(p, EnterPremises(unrestricted)) & Obl(p, EnterPremises(notice_24h)))

# ==============================================================================
# Note on Closed-World Assumption (CWA):
# "Missing clause" checks (e.g. absent deposit refund timeline, absent repair
# duty) operate via Negation-as-Failure over the extracted ClauseIR set,
# rather than open-world FOPL refutation.
# ==============================================================================
